  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting COVID-19 Response and Relief at the Country Level through Disbursement and Facilitation of Subgrants for Selected Diaspora Organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will support COVID-19 response in selected countries by providing sub-grants and coordination opportunities to vetted diaspora organizations to strengthen and facilitate the reach and effectiveness of diaspora initiatives in COVID-19 relief and recovery. Eligible projects will be funded, supported, and monitored by IOM both at the level of diasporas&#x2019; countries of residence and origin. The project aims to enhance COVID-19 response and recovery efforts by supporting diaspora interventions in their countries of origin, in coordination with local stakeholders. Through the identification of priority countries and needs on the ground with respect to COVID-19 relief and recovery, and in leveraging their human capital, financial contributions and community networks, selected diaspora organizations&#x2019; interventions will be supported via the subgrant in their process of scaling up existing initiatives. Subgrantees will operate and complement the COVID-19 relief and recovery efforts undertaken by local actors by proposing context specific solutions, including the support of health systems&#x2019; strengthening as relevant. Through the allocation and the implementation of the subgrants, the project seeks to promote mechanisms towards more effective coordination and communication opportunities among the different stakeholders involved in COVID-19 response including local and national governments, organizations, and diaspora.</narrative>
  </description>
